IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 33 and 34.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively): alteration of the objects in the constitution (s 33), and alteration of a constitution that contains the provisions
-- of s 10 of the Residential Property Act 1976 (s 34). The Residential Property Act 1976 is not among the sources: the fact that a provision is one it refers to is an input.
-- Periods are counted by sg-periods.l4 only. "21 days' written notice" is read as the notice given not less than 21 days before the meeting (P5); the clear-days reading (P7) is the other (fork line F-I12).
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 33(1) to (4): the resolution, the notice, and who must be given it`

-- (1): "Subject to this section, a company may by special resolution alter the provisions of its constitution with respect to the objects of the company, if any."
-- src:5639 | 33.—(1) Subject to this section, a company may by special
-- src:5640 | resolution alter the provisions of its constitution with respect to the
-- src:5641 | objects of the company, if any.
@ref s 33(1) (src:5639-5641)
GIVEN `the kind of resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution`
      `the constitution has provisions with respect to the objects of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) the company may alter the provisions of its constitution with respect to its objects by the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the constitution has provisions with respect to the objects of the company`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the kind of resolution`
          WHEN `a special resolution` THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may by special resolution alter" does not say that no other resolution will do (fork line F-I9)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the provisions of its constitution with respect to the objects of the company, if any" -- a constitution with no objects provisions has nothing for the subsection to alter

-- (2): "it must give 21 days' written notice by post or by electronic communications in accordance with section 387A or 387C, specifying the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution
-- and to submit it for passing at a meeting of the company to be held on a day specified in the notice." Counted by P5: given not later than 21 days before the day of the meeting.
-- src:5645 | (2) Where a company proposes to alter its constitution, with respect
-- src:5646 | to the objects of the company, it must give 21 days’ written notice by
-- src:5647 | post or by electronic communications in accordance with
-- src:5648 | section 387A or 387C, specifying the intention to propose the
-- src:5649 | resolution as a special resolution and to submit it for passing at a
-- src:5650 | meeting of the company to be held on a day specified in the notice.
@ref s 33(2) (src:5645-5650)
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting specified in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the notice is in writing and is given by post or by electronic communications in accordance with section 387A or 387C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution and to submit it for passing at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) the company has given the notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the notice is in writing and is given by post or by electronic communications in accordance with section 387A or 387C`
      AND `the notice specifies the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution and to submit it for passing at the meeting`
      AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the notice was given` `the day of the meeting specified in the notice` 21 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must give 21 days' written notice by post or by electronic communications in accordance with section 387A or 387C, specifying the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution and to submit it for passing at a meeting ... to be held on a day specified in the notice" (a duty not met, a period fixed in its own words; fork line F-I12)

DECLARE `s 33(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 33(2) give 21 days' written notice of the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. Time 0 is when the proposal is made; the last day for giving notice is 21 days before the meeting, counted in days from time 0.
-- src:5645 | (2) Where a company proposes to alter its constitution, with respect
-- src:5646 | to the objects of the company, it must give 21 days’ written notice by
-- src:5647 | post or by electronic communications in accordance with
-- src:5648 | section 387A or 387C, specifying the intention to propose the
-- src:5649 | resolution as a special resolution and to submit it for passing at a
-- src:5650 | meeting of the company to be held on a day specified in the notice.
@ref s 33(2) (src:5645-5650)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the last day for giving the notice, counted in days from the time the company proposes to alter its constitution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 33(2) act`
`s 33(2) the company must give 21 days' written notice` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 33(2) give 21 days' written notice of the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution`
    WITHIN `the last day for giving the notice, counted in days from the time the company proposes to alter its constitution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not give 21 days' written notice of the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution"

-- (3): "The notice must be given to all members, and to all trustees for debenture holders and, if there are no trustees for any class of debenture holders, to all debenture holders of that class whose names are, at the time of the posting of the notice, known to the company."
-- src:5654 | (3) The notice must be given to all members, and to all trustees for
-- src:5655 | debenture holders and, if there are no trustees for any class of
-- src:5656 | debenture holders, to all debenture holders of that class whose names
-- src:5657 | are, at the time of the posting of the notice, known to the company.
@ref s 33(3) (src:5654-5657)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee for debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a debenture holder of a class that has no trustee, and the company knew the person's name at the time of the posting of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(3) the notice must be given to the person` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a member of the company`
       OR `the person is a trustee for debenture holders`
       OR `the person is a debenture holder of a class that has no trustee, and the company knew the person's name at the time of the posting of the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be given to all members, and to all trustees for debenture holders and, if there are no trustees ..., to all debenture holders of that class whose names are ... known to the company" names three classes and says nothing of anyone else

-- (4): "The Court may in the case of any person or class of persons for such reasons as to it seem sufficient dispense with the notice required by subsection (2)."
-- src:5659 | (4) The Court may in the case of any person or class of persons for
-- src:5660 | such reasons as to it seem sufficient dispense with the notice required
-- src:5661 | by subsection (2).
@ref s 33(4) (src:5659-5661)
GIVEN `the Court considers the reasons sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(4) the Court may dispense with the notice for the person or class of persons` MEANS
    IF `the Court considers the reasons sufficient`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may ... for such reasons as to it seem sufficient dispense with the notice" -- a power whose gate (sufficient reasons) failed; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-I13)

§ `Section 33(5) to (7): the application to cancel the alteration`

-- (5A): "any of the company's issued shares held as treasury shares is to be disregarded" for the purposes of subsection (5).
-- src:5680 | (5A) For the purposes of subsection (5), any of the company’s
-- src:5681 | issued shares held as treasury shares is to be disregarded.
@ref s 33(5A) (src:5680-5681)
GIVEN `the number of issued shares of the company or of the class` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those issued shares that the company holds as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 33(5A) the number of issued shares counted for subsection (5)` MEANS
    `the number of issued shares of the company or of the class` MINUS `the number of those issued shares that the company holds as treasury shares`

-- (5)(a): "the holders of not less in the aggregate than 5% of the total number of issued shares of the company or any class of those shares or, if the company is not limited by shares, not less than 5% of the company's members".
-- A company is "limited by shares" in the sense of s 4(1) "company limited by shares" (sg-definitions.l4). 5% is tested as 100 times the part against 5 times the whole (no division).
-- src:5666 | (5) If an application for the cancellation of an alteration is made to
-- src:5667 | the Court in accordance with this section by —
-- src:5669 | (a) the holders of not less in the aggregate than 5% of the total
-- src:5670 | number of issued shares of the company or any class of
-- src:5671 | those shares or, if the company is not limited by shares, not
-- src:5672 | less than 5% of the company’s members; or
@ref s 33(5) (src:5666-5672)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the number of issued shares of the company or of the class that the applicants hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares of the company or of the class` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those issued shares that the company holds as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members of the company who are applicants` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(5)(a) the applicants hold enough of the shares, or are enough of the members` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "company limited by shares" the company is a company limited by shares` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF    `s 33(5A) the number of issued shares counted for subsection (5)` `the number of issued shares of the company or of the class` `the number of those issued shares that the company holds as treasury shares` GREATER THAN 0
             AND `the number of issued shares of the company or of the class that the applicants hold` TIMES 100 AT LEAST 5 TIMES `s 33(5A) the number of issued shares counted for subsection (5)` `the number of issued shares of the company or of the class` `the number of those issued shares that the company holds as treasury shares`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the holders of not less in the aggregate than 5% of the total number of issued shares of the company or any class of those shares" (a condition the text introduces with "if" on the application; treasury shares disregarded under (5A); reading (a) for a lawyer, fork line F-I4)
    ELSE (IF    `the number of members of the company` GREATER THAN 0
            AND `the number of members of the company who are applicants` TIMES 100 AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the number of members of the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company is not limited by shares, not less than 5% of the company's members" (reading (a), fork line F-I4)

-- (5)(b): "the holders of not less than 5% in nominal value of the company's debentures".
-- src:5674 | (b) the holders of not less than 5% in nominal value of the
-- src:5675 | company’s debentures,
@ref s 33(5)(b) (src:5674-5675)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the company's debentures that the applicants hold, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of all the company's debentures, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(5)(b) the applicants hold enough in nominal value of the company's debentures` MEANS
    IF    `the nominal value of all the company's debentures, in Singapore dollars` GREATER THAN 0
      AND `the nominal value of the company's debentures that the applicants hold, in Singapore dollars` TIMES 100 AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the nominal value of all the company's debentures, in Singapore dollars`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the holders of not less than 5% in nominal value of the company's debentures" (reading (a), fork line F-I4)

-- (6): "The application must be made within 21 days after the date on which the resolution altering the company's objects was passed" (P2: an act on any day up to the last day is in time).
-- src:5685 | (6) The application must be made within 21 days after the date on
-- src:5686 | which the resolution altering the company’s objects was passed, and
-- src:5687 | may be made on behalf of the persons entitled to make the application
-- src:5688 | by such one or more of their number as they appoint in writing for the
-- src:5689 | purpose.
@ref s 33(6) (src:5685-5689)
GIVEN `the day the resolution altering the company's objects was passed` IS A DATE
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(6) the application is made in time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the resolution altering the company's objects was passed` `the day the application was made` 21 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be made within 21 days after the date on which the resolution altering the company's objects was passed" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)

-- (6), second limb: the application "may be made on behalf of the persons entitled to make the application by such one or more of their number as they appoint in writing for the purpose".
-- src:5685 | (6) The application must be made within 21 days after the date on
-- src:5686 | which the resolution altering the company’s objects was passed, and
-- src:5687 | may be made on behalf of the persons entitled to make the application
-- src:5688 | by such one or more of their number as they appoint in writing for the
-- src:5689 | purpose.
@ref s 33(6) (src:5685-5689)
GIVEN `the applicants are one or more of the persons entitled to make the application, appointed in writing by them for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(6) the application may be made on behalf of the persons entitled by the applicants` MEANS
    IF `the applicants are one or more of the persons entitled to make the application, appointed in writing by them for the purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made on behalf of the persons entitled ... by such one or more of their number as they appoint in writing for the purpose" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I13)

-- (5): "If an application for the cancellation of an alteration is made to the Court in accordance with this section by (a) ...; or (b) ..., the alteration does not have effect except so far as it is confirmed by the Court."
-- src:5666 | (5) If an application for the cancellation of an alteration is made to
-- src:5667 | the Court in accordance with this section by —
-- src:5669 | (a) the holders of not less in the aggregate than 5% of the total
-- src:5670 | number of issued shares of the company or any class of
-- src:5671 | those shares or, if the company is not limited by shares, not
-- src:5672 | less than 5% of the company’s members; or
-- src:5674 | (b) the holders of not less than 5% in nominal value of the
-- src:5675 | company’s debentures,
-- src:5677 | the alteration does not have effect except so far as it is confirmed by
-- src:5678 | the Court.
@ref s 33(5) (src:5666-5678)
GIVEN `the applicants are within paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to the Court in accordance with this section, including within the 21 days of subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(5) the alteration does not have effect except so far as the Court confirms it` MEANS
    IF    `the applicants are within paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (5)`
      AND `the application is made to the Court in accordance with this section, including within the 21 days of subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application ... is made to the Court in accordance with this section by (a) ... or (b) ..., the alteration does not have effect except so far as it is confirmed by the Court" (a condition the text introduces with "If"; reading (a), fork line F-I4)

-- (7): "On the application, the Court (a) must have regard to the rights and interests of the members ... as well as to the rights and interests of the creditors; (b) may if it thinks fit adjourn ...; (c) may give such directions ...; (d) may make an order cancelling the alteration or confirming ...".
-- (a) is a duty of the Court gated by "On the application": JUST FALSE where there is no application (the periods ruling, items (b) and (c): "On" counts as "where"; limit 2 of the grant ruling: a duty). (b) to (d) are powers: NOTHING (the grant ruling, limit 1). Split sites (ii): F-I14.
