-- src:5693 | (a) must have regard to the rights and interests of the members
-- src:5694 | of the company or of any class of them as well as to the
-- src:5695 | rights and interests of the creditors;
@ref s 33(7)(a) (src:5691-5695)
GIVEN `the Court is hearing an application under section 33(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(7)(a) the Court must have regard to the rights and interests of the members and of the creditors` MEANS
    IF `the Court is hearing an application under section 33(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the application, the Court — (a) must have regard to ..." (a duty gated by "On the application"; split site (ii), fork line F-I14)

