-- src:5694 | of the company or of any class of them as well as to the
-- src:5695 | rights and interests of the creditors;
-- src:5697 | (b) may if it thinks fit adjourn the proceedings in order that an
-- src:5698 | arrangement may be made to the satisfaction of the Court
-- src:5699 | for the purchase (otherwise than by the company) of the
-- src:5700 | interests of dissentient members;
@ref s 33(7)(b) (src:5691-5700)
GIVEN `the Court is hearing an application under section 33(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is that an arrangement may be made to the satisfaction of the Court for the purchase, otherwise than by the company, of the interests of dissentient members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(7)(b) the Court may adjourn the proceedings` MEANS
    IF    `the Court is hearing an application under section 33(5)`
      AND `the Court thinks fit`
      AND `the purpose is that an arrangement may be made to the satisfaction of the Court for the purchase, otherwise than by the company, of the interests of dissentient members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the application, the Court ... (b) may if it thinks fit adjourn the proceedings in order that an arrangement may be made ..." -- a power whose gate failed (split site (ii), fork line F-I14)

