§ `Section 33(8) to (11): lodging, when the alteration takes effect, and "alteration"`

-- (8): "Despite any other provision of this Act, a copy of a resolution altering the objects of a company must not be lodged with the Registrar before the expiration of 21 days after the passing of the resolution,
-- or if any application to the Court has been made, before the application has been determined by the Court, whichever is the later." The 21 days expire at the end of the 21st day after the day of passing (P1), so the first day on which lodging is not barred is the 22nd.
-- A bar: JUST TRUE means lodging on that day is barred. Outside the bar the text does not say lodging is permitted (it is subsection (9)'s duty): NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only": the ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)).
-- src:5710 | (8) Despite any other provision of this Act, a copy of a resolution
-- src:5711 | altering the objects of a company must not be lodged with the
-- src:5716 | Registrar before the expiration of 21 days after the passing of the
-- src:5717 | resolution, or if any application to the Court has been made, before
-- src:5718 | the application has been determined by the Court, whichever is the
-- src:5719 | later.
@ref s 33(8) (src:5710-5719)
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `an application to the Court has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Court determined the application` IS A DATE
      `the day the copy would be lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(8) lodging the copy of the resolution on the day is barred` MEANS
    IF `the day the copy would be lodged` LESS THAN `s 33(8) the first day on which the copy may be lodged` `the day the resolution was passed` `an application to the Court has been made` `the day the Court determined the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says "must not be lodged ... before the expiration of 21 days ... whichever is the later"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on lodging "before" that day; on and after it the text does not say lodging is permitted (subsection (9) makes it a duty within 14 days)

GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `an application to the Court has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Court determined the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33(8) the first day on which the copy may be lodged` MEANS
    IF `an application to the Court has been made`
    THEN (IF `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed` 21 Days PLUS 1 GREATER THAN `the day the Court determined the application`
          THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed` 21 Days PLUS 1
          ELSE `the day the Court determined the application`)
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed` 21 Days PLUS 1

-- (9): "A copy of the resolution must be lodged with the Registrar by the company within 14 days after the expiration of the 21 days mentioned in subsection (8), but if an application has been made to the Court,
-- the copy must be lodged with the Registrar together with a copy of the order of the Court within 14 days after the application has been determined by the Court."
-- src:5721 | (9) A copy of the resolution must be lodged with the Registrar by
-- src:5722 | the company within 14 days after the expiration of the 21 days
-- src:5723 | mentioned in subsection (8), but if an application has been made to
-- src:5724 | the Court in accordance with this section, the copy must be lodged
-- src:5725 | with the Registrar together with a copy of the order of the Court
-- src:5726 | within 14 days after the application has been determined by the Court.
@ref s 33(9) (src:5721-5726)
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `an application to the Court has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Court determined the application` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged the copy with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company lodged the copy` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the order of the Court was lodged with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(9) the company has complied with the duty to lodge the copy of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company has lodged the copy with the Registrar`
    THEN (IF    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (IF `an application to the Court has been made` THEN `the day the Court determined the application` ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed` 21 Days) `the day the company lodged the copy` 14 Days
             AND ((NOT `an application to the Court has been made`) OR `a copy of the order of the Court was lodged with it`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be lodged with the Registrar by the company within 14 days after the expiration of the 21 days ..., but if an application has been made to the Court, the copy must be lodged ... together with a copy of the order of the Court within 14 days after the application has been determined" (a period fixed in its own words, outside it; a copy of the order missing)
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` (IF `an application to the Court has been made` THEN `the day the Court determined the application` ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed` 21 Days) 14 Days
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the 14 days have run and nothing is lodged
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 14 days have not run, and the text does not say the duty is met or unmet before then

DECLARE `s 33(9) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 33(9) lodge with the Registrar a copy of the resolution altering the objects (with a copy of the order of the Court, if an application has been made)`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. Time 0 is the day the 14 days run from: the day after the 21 days expire, or, where an application has been made, the day the application is determined.
-- src:5721 | (9) A copy of the resolution must be lodged with the Registrar by
-- src:5722 | the company within 14 days after the expiration of the 21 days
-- src:5723 | mentioned in subsection (8), but if an application has been made to
-- src:5724 | the Court in accordance with this section, the copy must be lodged
-- src:5725 | with the Registrar together with a copy of the order of the Court
-- src:5726 | within 14 days after the application has been determined by the Court.
@ref s 33(9) (src:5721-5726)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 33(9) act`
`s 33(9) the company must lodge a copy of the resolution within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 33(9) lodge with the Registrar a copy of the resolution altering the objects (with a copy of the order of the Court, if an application has been made)`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge a copy of the resolution altering its objects within 14 days after the 21 days expired or the application was determined"

-- (10): "On compliance by a company with subsection (9), the alteration (if any) of the objects takes effect."
-- src:5728 | (10) On compliance by a company with subsection (9), the
-- src:5729 | alteration (if any) of the objects takes effect.
@ref s 33(10) (src:5728-5729)
GIVEN `the company has complied with subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(10) the alteration of the objects takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the company has complied with subsection (9)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On compliance by a company with subsection (9), the alteration (if any) of the objects takes effect." ("On" counts as "where": the ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); reading (a) for a lawyer, fork line F-I4)

-- (11): "a reference in this section to the alteration of any provision of the constitution of a company or the alteration of the objects of a company includes the removal of that provision or of all or any of those objects."
-- src:5731 | (11) To avoid doubt, a reference in this section to the alteration of
-- src:5732 | any provision of the constitution of a company or the alteration of the
-- src:5733 | objects of a company includes the removal of that provision or of all
-- src:5734 | or any of those objects.
@ref s 33(11) (src:5731-5734)
GIVEN `the thing is the removal of the provision or of all or any of the objects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(11) the thing is within the word alteration` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the removal of the provision or of all or any of the objects`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the removal of that provision or of all or any of those objects" does not close the meaning

§ `Section 34: the constitution and section 10 of the Residential Property Act 1976`

-- (1): "Where the constitution of a company contains any of the provisions referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act 1976 in force immediately before 31 March 2006,
-- the company may, by special resolution, amend its constitution to remove that provision."
-- src:5742 | 34.—(1) Where the constitution of a company contains any of the
-- src:5743 | provisions referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property
-- src:5744 | Act 1976 in force immediately before 31 March 2006, the company
-- src:5745 | may, by special resolution, amend its constitution to remove that
-- src:5746 | provision.
@ref s 34(1) (src:5742-5746)
GIVEN `the constitution contains a provision referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act 1976 as in force immediately before 31 March 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) the company may amend its constitution to remove the provision` MEANS
    IF `the constitution contains a provision referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act 1976 as in force immediately before 31 March 2006`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the kind of resolution`
          WHEN `a special resolution` THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may, by special resolution, amend" does not say that no other resolution will do (fork line F-I9)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the constitution of a company contains any of the provisions referred to in section 10(1) ..." -- a power whose "Where" gate failed; split site (ii), fork line F-I15

-- (2)(a): "Where the constitution of a company contains a provision to the effect that its constitution must not be altered to remove any of the provisions referred to in section 10(1) ... except in accordance with the requirements of that Act —
-- (a) that provision ceases to have effect as from that date". "that date" is 31 March 2006.
`s 34 the day 31 March 2006` MEANS Date 31 3 2006

-- src:5750 | (2) Where the constitution of a company contains a provision to the
-- src:5751 | effect that its constitution must not be altered to remove any of the
-- src:5752 | provisions referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act
-- src:5753 | 1976 in force immediately before 31 March 2006 except in
-- src:5754 | accordance with the requirements of that Act —
-- src:5756 | (a) that provision ceases to have effect as from that date; and
@ref s 34(2)(a) (src:5750-5756)
GIVEN `the constitution contains a provision to the effect that it must not be altered to remove any of the provisions referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act 1976 except in accordance with the requirements of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2)(a) the provision has ceased to have effect` MEANS
    IF `the constitution contains a provision to the effect that it must not be altered to remove any of the provisions referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act 1976 except in accordance with the requirements of that Act`
    THEN (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `s 34 the day 31 March 2006`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that provision ceases to have effect as from that date" (a date the text fixes in its own words; before it the provision has effect)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks of "a provision to the effect that its constitution must not be altered to remove any of the provisions ... except in accordance with the requirements of that Act"

-- (2)(b): "the company may, by special resolution, amend its constitution to remove that provision."
-- src:5750 | (2) Where the constitution of a company contains a provision to the
-- src:5751 | effect that its constitution must not be altered to remove any of the
-- src:5752 | provisions referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act
-- src:5753 | 1976 in force immediately before 31 March 2006 except in
-- src:5754 | accordance with the requirements of that Act —
-- src:5756 | (a) that provision ceases to have effect as from that date; and
-- src:5758 | (b) the company may, by special resolution, amend its
-- src:5759 | constitution to remove that provision.
@ref s 34(2)(b) (src:5750-5759)
GIVEN `the constitution contains a provision to the effect that it must not be altered to remove any of the provisions referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act 1976 except in accordance with the requirements of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2)(b) the company may amend its constitution to remove that provision` MEANS
    IF `the constitution contains a provision to the effect that it must not be altered to remove any of the provisions referred to in section 10(1) of the Residential Property Act 1976 except in accordance with the requirements of that Act`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the kind of resolution`
          WHEN `a special resolution` THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may, by special resolution, amend" does not say that no other resolution will do (fork line F-I9)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the constitution of a company contains a provision to the effect that ..." -- a power whose "Where" gate failed; split site (ii), fork line F-I15
